ory about one  person but  also the origin story for a villain we  face in game this is just a taste of  some of the side quests the game has to  offer and i did not cherry pick these  quests  these were all located within the first  five or so areas of the game  and i still have a long way to go before  i beat this game's story as according to  some media sources there's around maybe  12 to 17 areas in the game to explore  which means  i have dozens of more side quests i  haven't even experienced yet  if you do want to get this game for  yourself it is playable on console and  pc  i would always highly recommend watching  reviews of gameplay and other mechanics  as this video has only showed  little of its story and not much else  but if you are dead set on getting this  game at the time of making this video  it's on pc playstation and xbox for  60 dollars or for free if you own xbox  game pass  outriders is an interesting game i  didn't think i was going to like this  game as looter shooters have never been  a genre i dump hours into but these  small side quests have pulled me in  enough to keep me going  something i did not expect to happen as  you wind down to the outro i want to  thank you all for joining me on this  journey while we look through some of  outrider's beautifully crafted side  quests and characters  if you want to see some more analysis or  essay style content like this i highly  recommend my recent uploads like  dishonored and the extreme power dynamic  between the rich and poor throughout the  series as well as my far cry upload  showcasing why far cry's villains are so  likable and well written  as always like the video and subscribe  if you're new if you're a returning  viewer i thank you for coming back for  another analysis video  thank you for watching and goodbye  [Music]  you
 

